  "slug": "phases-symtft-1132",
  "summary": "Recent preprints redefine protecting symmetries and invariants for lattice topological phases, including on fractal geometries.",
  "synthesis": "The common thread across these preprints is symmetry-constrained classification of lattice topological phases, in which the protecting symmetry or invariant is generalized. One study identifies phases protected by half-chiral symmetry, where chiral symmetry acts on one sublattice only, and characterizes them with real-space invariants and zero-energy modes. A second generalizes the spectral localizer to unify Z and Z2 invariants for hinge modes, Dirac nodes and valley boundary modes. A third realizes SSH, Haldane, Qi-Wu-Zhang and Z2 insulators on fractal lattices, including site-eliminated, projected and patterned constructions. What is new is the widening of protecting symmetries and invariants rather than a single shared method, with the fractal study transferring established models while the others redefine the controlling symmetry or invariant.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-26"
}
